defklown wrote:
> Can you name some specific things that one could do with #chat? What
> would it be useful for, that is.

Beware - some SPOILER !!!


The prevalent is chatting while in a shop to get information about the
prices; you need not be adjacent to the shopkeeper to do that.

To obtain hints/information about the game you may chat with the Oracle.

Chat with temple priests to buy intrinsic protection.

I think you may chat with your pets to obtain information about their
hunger status (but I can't tell anything about the pet's reply-code).

To enter your quest you may chat with your quest leader. Usually that
is triggered without explicit chatting (just approach), but there are
circumstances that the quest leader wanders around and chatting will
draw his attention.

Besides the above you may chat with any creature in the dungeons, but
mostly just for your amusement.

